Hi Justin,

Emma Howrilla in Durham Planning referred me to you (Infrastructure
Review). I'm doing due-diligence on a possible purchase of 1621
Clermont Rd, Durham 27713 (PIN 0728808242 / REID 153775, ~9.4 ac) and
need to understand the access requirement before going further.

Situation: the buildable ground is the upland corner fronting Clermont
Rd. The Clermont right-of-way in front of the parcel is unmaintained -the
the pavement dead-ends roughly 258 ft east of Euclid Rd. Sewer is
available via an on-site easement; water would need to be extended.

Questions:
1. For a single dwelling - or a duplex - on that frontage, would the
end of Clermont have to be built out to a public-street standard, or
can a private driveway off the existing pavement satisfy access? Yes, a Cit=
y street would need to be built along with extended the City water main und=
er the new street.
2. If a build-out is required, what standard applies (pavement width,
length to the site, turnaround/cul-de-sac, sidewalk)? That lets me
scope cost with a civil engineer. Extend the same width as the existing str=
eet along curb and gutter and sidewalk. If the street extension from the in=
tersection is more than 300' a permanent cul-de-sac would be required.
3. Does the answer change if I create one or two lots via a minor
subdivision vs. building on the existing single parcel? No, the answer woul=
d be the same.

I've attached a Durham GIS utility/ROW map and a parcel map showing
where the pavement ends. Happy to send anything else useful.

Thank you,
Kalin Ivanov

